## Execution Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    df[pandas.DataFrame] --> coordinator[DataFrameValidator]
    result[New ValidationResult] --> coordinator
    coordinator --> V1[RequiredColumnsValidator]
    V1 -- Updates result --> V2[DuplicateColumnsValidator]
    V2 -- Updates result --> V3[EmptyDatasetValidator]
    V3 -- Updates result --> V4[MissingValuesValidator]
    V4 -- Updates result --> V5[DataTypeValidator]
    V5 -- Updates result --> V6[BusinessRulesValidator]
    V6 --> Out[Return ValidationResult]
```

1. The client invokes `validator.validate(df)`.
2. A fresh `ValidationResult` object is instantiated.
3. The coordinator loops through each configured validator, passing `df` and the `ValidationResult` object.
4. Each validator appends its telemetry. If any validator appends an error to `result.errors`, the overall `result.is_valid` is set to `False`.
5. The populated `ValidationResult` is returned to the caller.

